      "file": "src/bin/fuzz/config_fuzzer.cc",
      "function": "LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput",
      "line": 53,
      "code": "config = config_open_for_fuzzing(static_data, size);",
      "note": "After truncating and copying the fuzz input into `static_data`, the harness dispatches that buffer into the project's config parser via `config_open_for_fuzzing()`.",
      "oracle_kind": "gt_parser_checkpoint",
      "kind": "parser_admitted"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/lib/lwan-config.c",
      "function": "config_open_for_fuzzing",
      "line": 771,
      "code": "return config_init_data(config, data, len);",
      "note": "First project-side consumption of the copied fuzz buffer and its clipped length: the fuzz-only helper starts config parsing on exactly `len` bytes from `data`.",
      "kind": "source"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/lib/lwan-config.c",
      "function": "config_init_data",
      "line": null,
      "code": ".end = (char *)data + len,",
      "note": "Root cause. Lexer initialization derives `lexer.end` from the full clipped fuzz length, so for this witness `lexer.end` becomes `static_data + 32768`, the first byte past the copied array. The later EOF lookahead in `peek()` steps back to and inspects that boundary. The staged fix avoids this state by having `config_open_for_fuzzing()` pass `len - 1`.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/lib/lwan-config.c",
      "function": "config_init_data",
      "line": 738,
      "code": ".end = (char *)data + len,",
